      "affected_item": "lem-nrqm-uncertainty-bounded-borel-calculus-of-commuting-operators",
      "affected_batch": "50",
      "status": "open",
      "routing": "owner-touched-alpha-obligation",
      "smallest_missing_requirement": "The proof establishes that F(Λ)=E_A(f⁻¹(Λ)) is a PVM, but does not establish that F is regular before invoking uniqueness to identify it with the spectral PVM of f(A). The cited thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators gives uniqueness among regular PVMs. Regularity follows because each scalar F-measure is finite Borel on ℝ; cite thm-locally-finite-borel-measures-are-regular-when-open-sets-are-sigma-compact and add the prerequisite, or prove regularity locally. Clause (c) is unproved as written; clause (a), used by the assigned joint-PVM criterion, is unaffected.",
      "original_finding": {
        "id": "lem-nrqm-uncertainty-bounded-borel-calculus-of-commuting-operators",
        "subject_type": "in-flight-item",
        "consumer_id": null,
        "observed_source": null,
        "location": "Proof, step 7.1, when uniqueness of the spectral PVM is invoked.",
        "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
        "evidence": "The proof establishes that F(Λ)=E_A(f⁻¹(Λ)) is a PVM, but does not establish that F is regular before invoking uniqueness to identify it with the spectral PVM of f(A). The cited thm-spectral-theorem-for-unbounded-self-adjoint-operators gives uniqueness among regular PVMs. Regularity follows because each scalar F-measure is finite Borel on ℝ; cite thm-locally-finite-borel-measures-are-regular-when-open-sets-are-sigma-compact and add the prerequisite, or prove regularity locally. Clause (c) is unproved as written; clause (a), used by the assigned joint-PVM criterion, is unaffected.",
        "severity": "nonfatal"
      },
