      "confirmed_status": "Current Proof7.1 proves the pushforward is a PVM and invokes uniqueness from the exact spectral theorem, but nowhere proves it regular. The supplied spectral theorem explicitly has uniqueness among regular PVMs.",
      "smallest_fix": "Add a cited regularity fact and a sentence immediately after F is shown to be a PVM: for each x, F_x is a finite positive Borel measure of mass ||x||^2, hence finite on compact sets; R is LCH and every open subset is sigma-compact, so the existing regularity theorem makes F_x regular. Therefore F is regular by the exact PVM definition before spectral uniqueness is used. The existing AC and Countable Choice hypotheses supply all choice needed.",
      "exact_available_prerequisites": [
        "lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm",
        "thm-locally-finite-borel-measures-are-regular-when-open-sets-are-sigma-compact",
